## Memory Governance
Before any persistent memory read, write, compress, or archive action, apply the `memory-rule` plugin skill.

Use the `memory-rule` plugin skill when:
- updating `MEMORY.md`
- writing to `notes/`
- promoting task facts into durable memory
- compressing or archiving completed work
- resolving conflicting preferences, rules, or corrections

`MEMORY.md` is a shared index, not the isolation boundary; per-task active files and worktree-local state isolate concurrent agent instances. If more than 3 instances are active, keep only the lead blocker, primary workstream, and a pointer to the full active roster here.
